    "content": "# Surah At-Takwir (التكوير) — The Overthrowing\n\nWelcome to the verse-by-verse Tafsir of **Surah At-Takwir**. This Surah forms an essential part of **Juz 'Amma (The 30th Part of the Holy Qur'an)**, revealed to awaken human conscience, establish the reality of eternal accountability, and ground the believer's daily life in sincere devotion to Allah.\n\n| Dimension | Details |\n|---|---|\n| **Surah Number** | 81 of 114 |\n| **Arabic Title** | سورة التكوير |\n| **English Meaning** | The Overthrowing |\n| **Classification** | Makki Revelation |\n| **Total Verses** | 29 Verses |\n| **Core Theme** | Cosmic cataclysm at the end of time, the questioning of the buried infant girl, and the absolute trustworthiness of revelation via the Angel Jibreel. |\n\n---\n\n## 1. Historical Revelation & Circumstances (Asbab an-Nuzul)\n\nRevealed to vividly awaken humanity to the universal dissolution of cosmic systems and the indisputable authenticity of the Prophetic message.\n\nScholars of Tafsir highlight that understanding the historical moment of revelation provides indispensable context for understanding why specific metaphors, warnings, and promises were selected by divine wisdom.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Complete Verse-by-Verse Exegesis (Tafsir)\n\n### Verses 1–14: The Twelve Cosmic Upheavals of the Final Hour\n\nThe sun folded up, stars falling, mountains swept away, pregnant camels neglected, wild beasts gathered, seas boiled over, souls reunited with bodies, and the buried female infant questioned about the crime for which she was slain.\n\n* **Linguistic Depth & Exegesis:** Classical commentaries (At-Tabari, Ibn Kathir, As-Sa'di) emphasize that these verses establish the unyielding moral responsibility of the human soul before its Creator, stripping away worldly distractions.\n\n---\n\n### Verses 15–29: Divine Oaths by the Stars, Dawn, and the Integrity of Revelation\n\nOaths by the retreating celestial planets, the departing night, and the breathing morning: the Qur'an is the word conveyed by an honorable, powerful messenger (Jibreel) upon the trustworthy Prophet Muhammad ﷺ.\n\n* **Linguistic Depth & Exegesis:** Classical commentaries (At-Tabari, Ibn Kathir, As-Sa'di) emphasize that these verses establish the unyielding moral responsibility of the human soul before its Creator, stripping away worldly distractions.\n\n\n---\n\n## 3. Essential Arabic Vocabulary & Linguistic Nuances\n\n- **Kuwwirat (كُوِّرَتْ)**: Folded up, wrapped, and stripped of its radiant light (describing the sun).\n- **Inkaddarat (ٱنكَدَرَتْ)**: Lost their brilliance and fell dispersing across the void (describing the stars).\n- **Suyyirat (سُيِّرَتْ)**: Moved forcefully and leveled into dust (describing the mountains).\n- **Al-Maw'udah (ٱلْمَوْءُۥدَةُ)**: The female infant buried alive in pre-Islamic Arabian barbaric custom.\n- **Kha-nas (الخُنَّسِ)**: The receding, stealthy stars that disappear in the morning light.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Practical Guidance Across All Stages of Life\n\nTo ensure the teachings of Surah At-Takwir transform our real-world character and daily relationships, classical scholars encourage tailoring its lessons across developmental stages:\n\n* 🧒 **For Children & Young Learners:** Allah created the sun, stars, and oceans, and He will recreate everything; always protect and care for babies and animals.\n* 🎒 **For Teenagers & Students:** Recognize that Islam eradicated barbaric misogyny and injustice long before modern movements.\n* 🏛️ **For Adults & Parents:** Realize that worldly order will dissolve in an instant; root your ultimate security only in Allah.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Practical Action Steps for Daily Life (Tadabbur wa 'Amal)\n\nTrue contemplation (*Tadabbur*) must always culminate in righteous action (*'Amal*):\n\n1. **Stand against all forms of injustice, especially against vulnerable children and women.**: Stand against all forms of injustice, especially against vulnerable children and women.\n2. **Recite Surah At-Takwir when you look at the night sky, reflecting on its eventual folding up.**: Recite Surah At-Takwir when you look at the night sky, reflecting on its eventual folding up.\n3. **Reaffirm your trust in the Noble Qur'an as divine speech conveyed by the trustworthy Angel Jibreel.**: Reaffirm your trust in the Noble Qur'an as divine speech conveyed by the trustworthy Angel Jibreel.\n",
