    "content": "# Surah Al-Infitar (الانفطار) — The Cleaving\n\nWelcome to the verse-by-verse Tafsir of **Surah Al-Infitar**. This Surah forms an essential part of **Juz 'Amma (The 30th Part of the Holy Qur'an)**, revealed to awaken human conscience, establish the reality of eternal accountability, and ground the believer's daily life in sincere devotion to Allah.\n\n| Dimension | Details |\n|---|---|\n| **Surah Number** | 82 of 114 |\n| **Arabic Title** | سورة الانفطار |\n| **English Meaning** | The Cleaving |\n| **Classification** | Makki Revelation |\n| **Total Verses** | 19 Verses |\n| **Core Theme** | The shattering of the sky, divine benevolence vs human ingratitude, the recording guardian angels (Kiram Katibin), and the finality of Yawm ad-Din. |\n\n---\n\n## 1. Historical Revelation & Circumstances (Asbab an-Nuzul)\n\nRevealed to confront human heedlessness and arrogance towards their Generous Creator who fashioned their anatomy in perfect symmetry.\n\nScholars of Tafsir highlight that understanding the historical moment of revelation provides indispensable context for understanding why specific metaphors, warnings, and promises were selected by divine wisdom.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Complete Verse-by-Verse Exegesis (Tafsir)\n\n### Verses 1–5: The Cleaving Skies and Awakening of the Soul\n\nWhen the sky cleaves apart, the stars scatter, the seas burst forth, and the graves are turned upside down, every soul will definitively know what it sent ahead and left behind.\n\n* **Linguistic Depth & Exegesis:** Classical commentaries (At-Tabari, Ibn Kathir, As-Sa'di) emphasize that these verses establish the unyielding moral responsibility of the human soul before its Creator, stripping away worldly distractions.\n\n---\n\n### Verses 6–12: Human Deception and the Guardian Scribes (Kiram Katibin)\n\nWhat has deceived man concerning his Generous Lord Who created, proportioned, and balanced him? Over each soul are appointed noble recording angels who know everything you do.\n\n* **Linguistic Depth & Exegesis:** Classical commentaries (At-Tabari, Ibn Kathir, As-Sa'di) emphasize that these verses establish the unyielding moral responsibility of the human soul before its Creator, stripping away worldly distractions.\n\n---\n\n### Verses 13–19: The Righteous in Bliss and the Sole Authority of Allah\n\nThe righteous dwell in eternal delight (Na'im) while the wicked burn in blazing fire (Jahim). That Day no soul possesses any power to aid another, and the command belongs entirely to Allah.\n\n* **Linguistic Depth & Exegesis:** Classical commentaries (At-Tabari, Ibn Kathir, As-Sa'di) emphasize that these verses establish the unyielding moral responsibility of the human soul before its Creator, stripping away worldly distractions.\n\n\n---\n\n## 3. Essential Arabic Vocabulary & Linguistic Nuances\n\n- **Infatarat (ٱنفَطَرَتْ)**: Cleaved, split, and ruptured asunder (the sky).\n- **Intatharat (ٱنتَثَرَتْ)**: Scattered in disorder (the stars).\n- **Fujjirat (فُجِّرَتْ)**: Burst forth and caused to overflow (the seas).\n- **Gharraka (غَرَّكَ)**: Deluded, deceived, and enticed you away.\n- **Kiram Katibin (كِرَامًا كَٰتِبِينَ)**: Noble, honorable scribes—the guardian angels who record every human deed.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Practical Guidance Across All Stages of Life\n\nTo ensure the teachings of Surah Al-Infitar transform our real-world character and daily relationships, classical scholars encourage tailoring its lessons across developmental stages:\n\n* 🧒 **For Children & Young Learners:** Allah created our eyes, ears, hands, and heart in perfect balance; remember that angels write down all our good deeds.\n* 🎒 **For Teenagers & Students:** Do not let worldly freedom deceive you into forgetting your Generous Lord; live with integrity in private and public.\n* 🏛️ **For Adults & Parents:** Recognize that divine generosity (Al-Karim) demands gratitude and obedience, not complacency and moral laxity.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Practical Action Steps for Daily Life (Tadabbur wa 'Amal)\n\nTrue contemplation (*Tadabbur*) must always culminate in righteous action (*'Amal*):\n\n1. **Say 'Alhamdulillah' when looking in the mirror, thanking Allah for fashioning your body in balanced proportion (82**: 7).\n2. **Be conscious of the Kiram Katibin recording your words, comments, and thoughts today.**: Be conscious of the Kiram Katibin recording your words, comments, and thoughts today.\n3. **Give charity quietly, seeking to have only righteous deeds registered in your eternal record.**: Give charity quietly, seeking to have only righteous deeds registered in your eternal record.\n",
