    "content": "# Surah At-Tariq (الطارق) — The Nightcomer\n\nWelcome to the verse-by-verse Tafsir of **Surah At-Tariq**. This Surah forms an essential part of **Juz 'Amma (The 30th Part of the Holy Qur'an)**, revealed to awaken human conscience, establish the reality of eternal accountability, and ground the believer's daily life in sincere devotion to Allah.\n\n| Dimension | Details |\n|---|---|\n| **Surah Number** | 86 of 114 |\n| **Arabic Title** | سورة الطارق |\n| **English Meaning** | The Nightcomer |\n| **Classification** | Makki Revelation |\n| **Total Verses** | 17 Verses |\n| **Core Theme** | The piercing celestial star, the guardian angel over every soul, human creation from gushing fluid as proof of resurrection, and the uncovering of innermost secrets. |\n\n---\n\n## 1. Historical Revelation & Circumstances (Asbab an-Nuzul)\n\nRevealed to establish empirical and biological evidence for the resurrection against Makkan skepticism.\n\nScholars of Tafsir highlight that understanding the historical moment of revelation provides indispensable context for understanding why specific metaphors, warnings, and promises were selected by divine wisdom.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Complete Verse-by-Verse Exegesis (Tafsir)\n\n### Verses 1–4: The Piercing Night Star and the Angelic Guardian\n\nOaths by the sky and the Night Star (At-Tariq)—the brilliant star piercing darkness: no soul exists except that it has a vigilant guardian angel assigned over it.\n\n* **Linguistic Depth & Exegesis:** Classical commentaries (At-Tabari, Ibn Kathir, As-Sa'di) emphasize that these verses establish the unyielding moral responsibility of the human soul before its Creator, stripping away worldly distractions.\n\n---\n\n### Verses 5–10: Human Origins and the Day Secrets are Exposed\n\nLet man consider from what he was created: from an ejected fluid issuing between the backbone and the ribs. Allah is fully able to resurrect him on the Day when all hidden secrets (As-Sara'ir) are laid bare.\n\n* **Linguistic Depth & Exegesis:** Classical commentaries (At-Tabari, Ibn Kathir, As-Sa'di) emphasize that these verses establish the unyielding moral responsibility of the human soul before its Creator, stripping away worldly distractions.\n\n---\n\n### Verses 11–17: The Decisive Word and the Ultimate Divine Stratagem\n\nOaths by the returning rain and the sprouting earth: the Qur'an is a decisive word, not mere amusement. The disbelievers plot their schemes, but Allah plans His divine response; leave them a short respite.\n\n* **Linguistic Depth & Exegesis:** Classical commentaries (At-Tabari, Ibn Kathir, As-Sa'di) emphasize that these verses establish the unyielding moral responsibility of the human soul before its Creator, stripping away worldly distractions.\n\n\n---\n\n## 3. Essential Arabic Vocabulary & Linguistic Nuances\n\n- **At-Tariq (الطَّارِقِ)**: That which arrives or knocks by night (the piercing celestial star).\n- **Ath-Thaqib (الثَّاقِبُ)**: Piercing, penetrating through darkness with intense brilliance.\n- **Dafiq (دَافِقٍ)**: Gushing, emitted forcefully (reproductive fluid).\n- **As-Sara'ir (السَّرَآئِرُ)**: The hidden secrets, concealed intentions, and private motives of the heart.\n- **Fasl (فَصْلٌ)**: Decisive, separating truth from falsehood with ultimate authority.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Practical Guidance Across All Stages of Life\n\nTo ensure the teachings of Surah At-Tariq transform our real-world character and daily relationships, classical scholars encourage tailoring its lessons across developmental stages:\n\n* 🧒 **For Children & Young Learners:** Allah created human beings from tiny beginnings; always be humble and know Allah knows our thoughts.\n* 🎒 **For Teenagers & Students:** Purify your private online habits and secret thoughts, knowing that secrets will be laid bare on Judgment Day.\n* 🏛️ **For Adults & Parents:** Recognize the decisive authority of the Qur'an; it is not amusement or light philosophy, but divine reality.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Practical Action Steps for Daily Life (Tadabbur wa 'Amal)\n\nTrue contemplation (*Tadabbur*) must always culminate in righteous action (*'Amal*):\n\n1. **Align your public actions with your private life so there is no shame when secrets are exposed (*Tubla as-Sara'ir*).**: Align your public actions with your private life so there is no shame when secrets are exposed (*Tubla as-Sara'ir*).\n2. **Contemplate the biological miracle of human conception as a daily reminder of Allah's resurrection power.**: Contemplate the biological miracle of human conception as a daily reminder of Allah's resurrection power.\n3. **Give breathing room and patience (*Mahhilhum ruwayda*) when dealing with foolish critics of faith.**: Give breathing room and patience (*Mahhilhum ruwayda*) when dealing with foolish critics of faith.\n",
