    "content": "# Surah Al-Ma'un (الماعون) — Small Kindnesses\n\nWelcome to the verse-by-verse Tafsir of **Surah Al-Ma'un**. This Surah forms an essential part of **Juz 'Amma (The 30th Part of the Holy Qur'an)**, revealed to awaken human conscience, establish the reality of eternal accountability, and ground the believer's daily life in sincere devotion to Allah.\n\n| Dimension | Details |\n|---|---|\n| **Surah Number** | 107 of 114 |\n| **Arabic Title** | سورة الماعون |\n| **English Meaning** | Small Kindnesses |\n| **Classification** | Makki Revelation |\n| **Total Verses** | 7 Verses |\n| **Core Theme** | The inseparable link between genuine religious faith and social compassion; condemnation of hypocrites who perform ostentatious prayer while mistreating orphans and withholding simple everyday aid. |\n\n---\n\n## 1. Historical Revelation & Circumstances (Asbab an-Nuzul)\n\nRevealed addressing pagan aristocrats like Abu Sufyan and Al-'As ibn Wa'il who rebuffed orphans and destitute beggars, as well as warning hypocrites in Madinah who prayed only to be seen by peers while withholding minor neighbourly utensils.\n\nScholars of Tafsir highlight that understanding the historical moment of revelation provides indispensable context for understanding why specific metaphors, warnings, and promises were selected by divine wisdom.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Complete Verse-by-Verse Exegesis (Tafsir)\n\n### Verses 1–3: The Denial of Judgment and Repelling the Orphan\n\nHave you seen the one who denies the final Recompense? That is the one who repulses the orphan harshly and does not encourage the feeding of the poor.\n\n* **Linguistic Depth & Exegesis:** Classical commentaries (At-Tabari, Ibn Kathir, As-Sa'di) emphasize that these verses establish the unyielding moral responsibility of the human soul before its Creator, stripping away worldly distractions.\n\n---\n\n### Verses 4–7: The Heedless, Ostentatious Worshipers Who Withhold Aid\n\nSo woe to those worshipers who are heedless of their prayer—those who make a show of their deeds and withhold simple neighbourly assistance (Al-Ma'un).\n\n* **Linguistic Depth & Exegesis:** Classical commentaries (At-Tabari, Ibn Kathir, As-Sa'di) emphasize that these verses establish the unyielding moral responsibility of the human soul before its Creator, stripping away worldly distractions.\n\n\n---\n\n## 3. Essential Arabic Vocabulary & Linguistic Nuances\n\n- **Yukadhdhibu bid-Din (يُكَذِّبُ بِٱلدِّينِ)**: Denies and rejects the ultimate Day of Judgment and divine retribution.\n- **Yadu''u al-Yatim (يَدُعُّ ٱلْيَتِيمَ)**: Violently repels, scolds, and deprives the helpless orphan of love and rights.\n- **Sahun (سَاهُونَ)**: Heedless, unmindful, lazy, and careless regarding their prayers and their prescribed times.\n- **Yura'un (يُرَآءُونَ)**: Acting ostentatiously to show off, gain applause, and impress onlookers (Riya').\n- **Al-Ma'un (ٱلْمَاعُونَ)**: Small, basic everyday necessities and neighbourly acts of kindness (salt, water, tools, pots).\n\n---\n\n## 4. Practical Guidance Across All Stages of Life\n\nTo ensure the teachings of Surah Al-Ma'un transform our real-world character and daily relationships, classical scholars encourage tailoring its lessons across developmental stages:\n\n* 🧒 **For Children & Young Learners:** Be kind to friends who don't have parents or toys; always share your tools, pencils, and snacks.\n* 🎒 **For Teenagers & Students:** Praying on time matters, but so does treating vulnerable people with dignity; avoid showing off on social media.\n* 🏛️ **For Adults & Parents:** Never separate ritual worship from moral ethics; ostentatious prayer is worthless if combined with coldhearted stinginess.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Practical Action Steps for Daily Life (Tadabbur wa 'Amal)\n\nTrue contemplation (*Tadabbur*) must always culminate in righteous action (*'Amal*):\n\n1. **Regularly sponsor or contribute to an orphan care initiative and visit vulnerable community members.**: Regularly sponsor or contribute to an orphan care initiative and visit vulnerable community members.\n2. **Never refuse a neighbour who asks to borrow a basic household item or utensil (salt, tools, ladder).**: Never refuse a neighbour who asks to borrow a basic household item or utensil (salt, tools, ladder).\n3. **Purify your intentions before every prayer to eliminate showing off (Riya'), praying strictly for Allah.**: Purify your intentions before every prayer to eliminate showing off (Riya'), praying strictly for Allah.\n",
